--TEST--
`&value` as an array-literal element is `E0483` at every depth, never a panic — `rule:types/implicit-capture` removed by-reference capture and `rule:classes/two-copy-depths` makes an element a copy, so an aliasing element has no owner in either
--FILE--
<?nvs
string $x = "a";
// `rule:types/implicit-capture` removed by-reference capture, so no binding aliases
// another: this element is a copy of `$x` taken where the literal is
// evaluated, and there is nothing for a write to travel back through.
array<string> $a = [&$x];
// The `&` sits on the value, so an element carrying an explicit key
// takes the identical refusal.
array<string> $b = ["k" => &$x];
// Every element list is walked at every depth — an inner literal is an
// element of the outer one, so a nested `&` is reported here rather than
// surviving to `nvs-ir` as a panic.
array<array<string>> $c = [["n" => &$x]];
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0483]: an array element cannot be taken by reference
  --> %s:6:21
  |
6 | array<string> $a = [&$x];
  |                     ^^^ this element is `&value`
  = help: Novis has no references: `rule:types/implicit-capture` removed by-reference capture and `rule:classes/two-copy-depths` makes an element a copy, so drop the `&` — to share one mutable cell, hold it in an object and store that

